From 89b885fd4acdebba0c9e9c4f130049e23b6fd0a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Donald Posterick <donny.p@live.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 12:44:48 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] stream: do not clamp the media channel buffer to the MTU

create_channel clamped channel->buf_size down to PJMEDIA_MAX_MTU minus
PJMEDIA_STREAM_RESV_PAYLOAD_LEN, on the assumption that an RTP payload
always fits inside the MTU. That assumption does not hold for
high-bitrate uncompressed codecs.

L16 at 44.1 kHz stereo produces 1764-byte frames at its 10 ms ptime:

  44100 * 2 channels * 2 bytes * 10 ms / 1000 = 1764

The encoder writes into channel->buf and trusts channel->buf_size to be
the real allocation, so once the clamp reduces it below the codec's frame
size the encode loop walks past the end and the process segfaults. Any
codec whose max_bps * ptime exceeds the MTU is affected.

The caller has already sized buf_size to what the codec needs, so the
allocation should match it. If the resulting packet exceeds the network
MTU, IP fragmentation handles it on the transport path; that is separate
from how much memory the encode target needs.

Applied on top of 2.17, which still carries the clamp unchanged.
---
 pjmedia/src/pjmedia/stream_imp_common.c | 16 ++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/pjmedia/src/pjmedia/stream_imp_common.c b/pjmedia/src/pjmedia/stream_imp_common.c
index 2dbbd3723..4a9542182 100755
--- a/pjmedia/src/pjmedia/stream_imp_common.c
+++ b/pjmedia/src/pjmedia/stream_imp_common.c
@@ -214,12 +214,16 @@ static pj_status_t create_channel( pj_pool_t *pool,
     /* Also include RTP header size (for sending) */
     channel->buf_size += sizeof(pjmedia_rtp_hdr);
 
-    if (channel->buf_size > PJMEDIA_MAX_MTU -
-                                PJMEDIA_STREAM_RESV_PAYLOAD_LEN)
-    {
-        channel->buf_size = PJMEDIA_MAX_MTU -
-                                PJMEDIA_STREAM_RESV_PAYLOAD_LEN;
-    }
+    /* NOTE: previously this block clamped channel->buf_size down to
+     * PJMEDIA_MAX_MTU - PJMEDIA_STREAM_RESV_PAYLOAD_LEN. That caused a
+     * buffer overrun in the encoder for any codec whose natural frame
+     * size exceeds the MTU (L16/44100 stereo at 10 ms ptime produces
+     * 1764 bytes per frame, larger than the default 1480-byte cap).
+     * `buf_size` as passed in by the caller already reflects the
+     * codec's actual max frame size (see stream.c: pjmedia_stream_create
+     * uses PJ_MAX of receive-side frame_size and codec max-bps-based
+     * estimate), so allocating exactly that much is correct. IP
+     * fragmentation on the send path handles >MTU RTP packets. */
 
     channel->buf = pj_pool_alloc(pool, channel->buf_size);
     PJ_ASSERT_RETURN(channel->buf != NULL, PJ_ENOMEM);
-- 
2.53.0

